IMPORT prelude

-- Internal Revenue Code of 1986 (26 U.S.C.) -- the individual's federal income tax, taxable year 2026. Seat-neutral core.
--
-- Encoded from the OLRC USLM text at release point Public Law 119-121 (current through 9 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/: usc26-ch1-schA-ptI.txt (ss 1, 2), usc26-ch1-schA-ptIV-sptA-C.txt (ss 24, 26, 31, 32),
-- usc26-ch1-schA-ptVI.txt (s 55, as a screen only), usc26-ch1-schB-ptI-III.txt (ss 61, 62, 63, 85, 86),
-- usc26-ch1-schB-ptV-VII-sel.txt (ss 151, 152, 164(f)), usc26-ch2.txt (ss 1401, 1402), usc26-ss6012-6013-7703.txt.
-- The figures for 2026 come from Rev. Proc. 2025-32 (irs-rev-proc-2025-32.txt), and the 2026 OASDI contribution and
-- benefit base from the SSA's notice at 90 FR 49047, deposited in ../../../social-security-act/registers/source-bundle/.
--
-- The rules are written in the Code's own actors and terms: "the taxpayer", "the spouse", "the individual". The questions an
-- individual asks are in irc-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module.
--
-- Read with ../../../social-security-act/ (Title II benefits, which s 86 makes partly taxable; another encoding links here).
-- The stable l4 cannot IMPORT across encoding folders, so that link is recorded in NOTES.md, not in code.
--
-- Not for public use as advice.

§ `Internal Revenue Code of 1986 -- the individual's federal income tax for 2026`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that can reach a gap answers `not covered` with one of these reasons.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- The dated tables below are those of Rev. Proc. 2025-32, for taxable years beginning in 2026 only.
    `the figures of a taxable year other than 2026 are not deposited`
    -- s 2(d), s 6013(g), (h), s 871: a nonresident alien is taxed under rules not encoded.
    `a nonresident alien is taxed under s 871 and s 877, which are not encoded`
    -- s 1(h): the maximum capital gains rate is deposited but its subchapter P definitions are not.
    `net capital gain and qualified dividends are taxed under s 1(h), which is not encoded`
    -- s 1(g): the tax on a child's unearned income.
    `the s 1(g) tax on a child's unearned income is not encoded`
    -- s 55: screened with an upper bound on alternative minimum taxable income; above the screen it is not encoded.
    `the alternative minimum tax under s 55 may apply, and it is not encoded beyond a screen`
    -- s 6017: the return a self-employed individual must make; not deposited.
    `s 6017 (returns of self-employment tax) may require a return, and it is not deposited`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the positive part of` x MEANS max 0 x

§§ `The facts of one taxable year`

-- One case is one individual's taxable year: the calendar year 2026, with the individual's spouse (if any) and the people
-- who live with the individual. On a joint return the two spouses are "the taxpayer" together (s 6013(d)(3)).

-- s 152(c)(2), (d)(2), (f)(1): how a person is related to the taxpayer. The list is the union of the relationships named in
-- s 2(a)(1)(B), s 2(b)(1)(B), s 152(c)(2) and s 152(d)(2).
DECLARE `Relationship to the taxpayer` IS ONE OF
    -- s 152(f)(1)(A)(i), (B): a son, daughter, stepson or stepdaughter, including a legally adopted child
    `a son, daughter, stepson or stepdaughter`
    -- s 152(f)(1)(A)(ii), (C): an eligible foster child, placed by an authorised agency or by court order
    `an eligible foster child`
    -- s 152(c)(2)(A), (d)(2)(A): "a descendant of such a child"
    `a grandchild or other descendant of a child`
    -- s 152(c)(2)(B), (d)(2)(B)
    `a brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister`
    -- s 152(c)(2)(B); s 152(d)(2)(E) names only "a son or daughter of a brother or sister"
    `a descendant of a brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(C); s 2(b)(1)(B) names "the father or mother"
    `the father or mother`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(C): "an ancestor of either"
    `a grandparent or other ancestor`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(D)
    `a stepfather or stepmother`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(F)
    `a brother or sister of the father or mother`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(G)
    `a son-in-law, daughter-in-law, father-in-law, mother-in-law, brother-in-law or sister-in-law`
    -- s 152(d)(2)(H): not a spouse, same principal place of abode for the year, a member of the household
    `an unrelated member of the household for the whole year`
    `none of these`

-- One person who may be the taxpayer's dependent.
DECLARE `Person` HAS
    `relationship`                                            IS A `Relationship to the taxpayer`
    -- s 152(c)(3): age "as of the close of the calendar year"
    `age at the close of the year`                            IS A NUMBER
    -- s 152(c)(3)(A)(ii), (f)(2): a full-time student during some part of each of 5 calendar months
    `a student`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(c)(3)(B), s 22(e)(3)
    `permanently and totally disabled`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(c)(1)(B), s 2(b)(1)(A): months of the year in which the person had the same principal place of abode
    `months sharing the taxpayer's home`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 32(c)(3)(C): that home was in the United States
    `the shared home was in the United States`                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(c)(1)(D)
    `provided over half of their own support`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(b)(2), (c)(1)(E)
    `made a joint return with a spouse`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `that joint return was only a claim of refund`            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(b)(1)(A)(i)(I), s 32(c)(3)(B)
    `married at the close of the year`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(b)(3)(A), s 24(c)(2), s 24(h)(4)(B)
    `a citizen or national of the United States`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a resident of the United States`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a resident of Canada or Mexico`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(d)(1)(B)
    `gross income for the calendar year`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 152(d)(1)(C), (d)(3)
    `the taxpayer provided over half of their support`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(c)(4): the tie-breaker gives the person to another taxpayer (asked as a fact)
    `treated as another taxpayer's qualifying child under s 152(c)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 152(d)(1)(D): a qualifying child of any other taxpayer
    `a qualifying child of another taxpayer`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 24(h)(7)(B), s 32(m): issued by the SSA to a citizen or for work, before the return's due date
    `has a social security number valid for employment`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- The individual's marriage. All the fields are about the taxpayer's spouse, if there is one.
DECLARE `Marriage` HAS
    -- s 7703(a)(1): married at the close of the year or, if the spouse died during the year, at the time of death
    `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse died during the year`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7703(a)(2), s 2(b)(2)(A), s 6013(d)(2)
    `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(b)(2)(B), s 6013(a)(1)
    `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7703(b)(3), s 32(d)(2)(B)(iii)(I)
    `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 86(c)(1)(C)(ii)
    `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6012(a)(1)(A)(iv)
    `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6013(a): the election to make a single return jointly
    `the spouses make a joint return`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6012(a)(1)(A), last sentence
    `the spouse makes a separate return`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 63(c)(6)(A)
    `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse's age at the close of the year`               IS A NUMBER
    `the spouse is blind`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 151(b)
    `the spouse has gross income`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 151(b), s 6012(a)(1)(A), last sentence
    `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(a)(1)(A): an earlier spouse died during either of the two preceding taxable years
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(a)(2)(A)
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(a)(2)(B)
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Amounts for the year, in US dollars. On a joint return the amounts are the couple's together, except the amounts split
-- between the taxpayer and the spouse because ss 1401-1402 and s 3101 apply to each individual.
DECLARE `Income` HAS
    -- s 61(a)(1), s 32(c)(2)(A)(i): wages, salaries, tips and other employee compensation includible in gross income
    `wages of the taxpayer`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `wages of the spouse`                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- s 61(a)(4); s 32(i)(2)(A)
    `taxable interest`                                        IS A NUMBER
    -- s 86(b)(2)(B), s 6012(d), s 32(i)(2)(B)
    `tax-exempt interest`                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- s 61(a)(7): dividends other than qualified dividends
    `ordinary dividends`                                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 1(h): not encoded; any amount answers not covered
    `qualified dividends and net capital gain`                IS A NUMBER
    -- s 61(a)(8), (10): the taxable part of pensions and annuities
    `taxable pensions and annuities`                          IS A NUMBER
    -- s 85
    `unemployment compensation`                               IS A NUMBER
    -- s 86(d): Title II monthly benefits and tier 1 railroad retirement benefits received, less repayments in the year
    `social security benefits`                                IS A NUMBER
    -- s 61(a): any other gross income
    `other gross income`                                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 61(a)(2), s 1402(a): gross income from a trade or business the individual carries on, and its deductions
    `business gross income of the taxpayer`                   IS A NUMBER
    `business deductions of the taxpayer`                     IS A NUMBER
    `business gross income of the spouse`                     IS A NUMBER
    `business deductions of the spouse`                       IS A NUMBER
    -- s 62(a): the other deductions allowed in arriving at adjusted gross income (not s 164(f), which is computed)
    `other deductions in arriving at adjusted gross income`   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 63(b)(3) to (8): ss 199A, 170(p), 224, 225 and the others the paragraph lists (not the standard deduction or s 151)
    `other deductions allowed to a non-itemizer`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 63(d), (e)
    `the taxpayer elects to itemize`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemized deductions`                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- s 24(d)(2)(A)(i): taxes imposed by s 3101 (and s 3201(a)) on amounts received
    `social security taxes withheld from wages`               IS A NUMBER
    -- s 31(a)
    `income tax withheld`                                     IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Taxable year` HAS
    -- the calendar year in which the taxable year begins
    `the calendar year`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`             IS A NUMBER
    -- s 63(f)(2), (4)
    `the taxpayer is blind`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(b)(3)(A), s 2(d)
    `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 151(d)(2), s 63(c)(5), s 152(b)(1), s 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(III)
    `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 32(c)(1)(B)
    `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(I)
    `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 2(a)(1), s 2(b)(1), s 7703(b)(2): "over half of the cost of maintaining the household"
    `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household` IS A BOOLEAN
    `marriage`                                                IS A `Marriage`
    `people`                                                  IS A LIST OF `Person`
    `income`                                                  IS AN `Income`

-- A marriage-free placeholder for a taxpayer with no spouse: no field of it is read once the first field is FALSE.
`no marriage` MEANS `Marriage` WITH
    `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death` IS FALSE
    `the spouse died during the year`                         IS FALSE
    `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`   IS FALSE
    `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouses make a joint return`                         IS FALSE
    `the spouse makes a separate return`                      IS FALSE
    `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`     IS FALSE
    `the spouse's age at the close of the year`               IS 0
    `the spouse is blind`                                     IS FALSE
    `the spouse has gross income`                             IS FALSE
    `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`         IS FALSE
    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS FALSE
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS FALSE
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS FALSE

§§ `s 7703 -- determination of marital status`

-- s 7703(a): "the determination of whether an individual is married shall be made as of the close of his taxable year;
-- except that if his spouse dies during his taxable year such determination shall be made as of the time of such death; and
-- (2) an individual legally separated from his spouse under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance shall not be
-- considered as married."
GIVEN m IS A `Marriage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `married under s 7703(a)` m IF
        m's `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death`
    AND (NOT m's `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance`)

§§ `s 152 -- dependent defined`

-- s 152(c)(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bears a qualifying child relationship` p IF
        p's `relationship` EQUALS `a son, daughter, stepson or stepdaughter`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `an eligible foster child`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a grandchild or other descendant of a child`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a descendant of a brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister`

-- s 152(c)(3): younger than the taxpayer and under 19, or a student under 24; or permanently and totally disabled.
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, `taxpayer's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the age requirements` p `taxpayer's age` IF
        p's `permanently and totally disabled`
    OR  (    p's `age at the close of the year` LESS THAN `taxpayer's age`
         AND (    p's `age at the close of the year` LESS THAN 19
              OR  (p's `a student` AND p's `age at the close of the year` LESS THAN 24)))

-- s 152(c)(1)(B): "the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year"
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `shares the taxpayer's home for more than half the year` p IF
    p's `months sharing the taxpayer's home` GREATER THAN 6

-- s 152(c)(1)(E): "has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund)"
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filed a joint return that counts under s 152(c)(1)(E)` p IF
    p's `made a joint return with a spouse` AND (NOT p's `that joint return was only a claim of refund`)

-- s 152(c)(1), with the s 152(c)(4) tie-breaker asked as a fact. The support test (D) is a parameter because s 32(c)(3)(A)
-- applies s 152(c) "without regard to paragraph (1)(D)".
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, `taxpayer's age` IS A NUMBER, `apply the support test` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p `taxpayer's age` `apply the support test` IF
        `bears a qualifying child relationship` p
    AND `shares the taxpayer's home for more than half the year` p
    AND `meets the age requirements` p `taxpayer's age`
    AND ((NOT `apply the support test`) OR (NOT p's `provided over half of their own support`))
    AND (NOT `filed a joint return that counts under s 152(c)(1)(E)` p)
    AND (NOT p's `treated as another taxpayer's qualifying child under s 152(c)(4)`)

-- s 152(d)(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bears a qualifying relative relationship` p IF
        `bears a qualifying child relationship` p
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `the father or mother`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a grandparent or other ancestor`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a stepfather or stepmother`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a brother or sister of the father or mother`
    OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `a son-in-law, daughter-in-law, father-in-law, mother-in-law, brother-in-law or sister-in-law`
    OR  (    p's `relationship` EQUALS `an unrelated member of the household for the whole year`
         AND p's `months sharing the taxpayer's home` AT LEAST 12)

-- s 152(d)(1)(B): "less than the exemption amount (as defined in section 151(d))". Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.23: "For taxable
-- years beginning in 2026, the exemption amount referred to in § 152(d)(1)(B) is $5,300." (See NOTES.md finding 1 on what
-- "exemption amount" means after s 151(d)(5)(A).)
`the 2026 exemption amount referred to in s 152(d)(1)(B)` MEANS 5300

-- s 152(d)(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, `taxpayer's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying relative under s 152(d)` p `taxpayer's age` IF
        `bears a qualifying relative relationship` p
    AND p's `gross income for the calendar year` LESS THAN `the 2026 exemption amount referred to in s 152(d)(1)(B)`
    AND p's `the taxpayer provided over half of their support`
    AND (NOT `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p `taxpayer's age` TRUE)
    AND (NOT p's `a qualifying child of another taxpayer`)

-- s 152(b)(3)(A): not a citizen or national unless a resident of the United States or of a contiguous country. The adopted
-- child exception in (b)(3)(B) is not encoded.
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the citizenship or residence test of s 152(b)(3)` p IF
        p's `a citizen or national of the United States`
    OR  p's `a resident of the United States`
    OR  p's `a resident of Canada or Mexico`

-- s 24(c)(2), s 24(h)(4)(B): s 152(b)(3)(A) "applied without regard to all that follows 'resident of the United States'"
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the s 24 citizenship or residence test` p IF
    p's `a citizen or national of the United States` OR p's `a resident of the United States`

-- s 152(a), (b): a qualifying child or a qualifying relative, unless the taxpayer is a dependent of another (b)(1), the
-- person made a joint return (b)(2), or fails the citizenship test (b)(3).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p IF
        (    `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`) TRUE
         OR  `a qualifying relative under s 152(d)` p (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`))
    AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`)
    AND (NOT p's `made a joint return with a spouse`)
    AND `meets the citizenship or residence test of s 152(b)(3)` p

§§ `s 2 -- surviving spouse and head of household`

-- s 2(a)(1)(B): a dependent "who ... is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer" (s 152 applied without
-- (b)(1), (b)(2), (d)(1)(B)), whose principal place of abode is the household "for the taxable year", and for whom the
-- taxpayer is entitled to a s 151 deduction. Read as: the whole year.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a child who qualifies the taxpayer as a surviving spouse` ty p IF
        p's `relationship` EQUALS `a son, daughter, stepson or stepdaughter`
    AND p's `months sharing the taxpayer's home` AT LEAST 12
    AND `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a surviving spouse under s 2(a)` ty IF
        ty's `marriage`'s `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `a child who qualifies the taxpayer as a surviving spouse` ty p) (ty's `people`)
    AND ty's `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household`
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`)
    AND ty's `marriage`'s `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death`

-- s 7703(b): a married individual who files a separate return, maintains a home that is for more than half the year the
-- principal place of abode of a child (s 152(f)(1)) for whom the individual is entitled to a s 151 deduction, furnishes over
-- half its cost, and whose spouse is not a member of the household in the last 6 months, "shall not be considered as
-- married". The "but for section 152(e)" limb is not encoded.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a child who keeps a separated taxpayer unmarried` ty p IF
        (    p's `relationship` EQUALS `a son, daughter, stepson or stepdaughter`
         OR  p's `relationship` EQUALS `an eligible foster child`)
    AND `shares the taxpayer's home for more than half the year` p
    AND `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treated as not married under s 7703(b)` ty IF
        `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouses make a joint return`)
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `a child who keeps a separated taxpayer unmarried` ty p) (ty's `people`)
    AND ty's `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household`
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year`)

-- s 2(b)(2), (c): married at the close of the year for s 2(b). Legally separated: not married (A). Spouse a nonresident
-- alien at any time: not married (B). Spouse died during the year: married (C). Treated as not married under s 7703(b) (c).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `married at the close of the year for s 2(b)` ty IF
        `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`)
    AND (NOT `treated as not married under s 7703(b)` ty)

-- s 2(b)(1)(A)(i): a qualifying child (s 152(c), without s 152(e)), but not one who is married at the close of the year and
-- is not a dependent by reason of s 152(b)(2) or (b)(3).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying person for head of household under s 2(b)(1)(A)` ty p IF
        `shares the taxpayer's home for more than half the year` p
    AND (    (    `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`) TRUE
              AND (NOT (    p's `married at the close of the year`
                        AND (    p's `made a joint return with a spouse`
                             OR  (NOT `meets the citizenship or residence test of s 152(b)(3)` p)))))
         -- (ii) any other dependent for whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction; s 2(b)(3)(B): not one who is a
         -- dependent only under s 152(d)(2)(H) or (d)(3) (multiple support is not encoded, so (H) only)
         OR  (    `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p
              AND (NOT p's `relationship` EQUALS `an unrelated member of the household for the whole year`)))

-- s 2(b)(1)(B): the household is the principal place of abode of the father or mother, for whom the taxpayer is entitled to
-- a deduction. The parent need not live with the taxpayer.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent who qualifies the taxpayer as head of household under s 2(b)(1)(B)` ty p IF
        p's `relationship` EQUALS `the father or mother`
    AND `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a head of household under s 2(b)` ty IF
        (NOT `married at the close of the year for s 2(b)` ty)
    AND (NOT `a surviving spouse under s 2(a)` ty)
    AND (    any (GIVEN p YIELD `a qualifying person for head of household under s 2(b)(1)(A)` ty p) (ty's `people`)
         OR  any (GIVEN p YIELD `a parent who qualifies the taxpayer as head of household under s 2(b)(1)(B)` ty p) (ty's `people`))
    AND ty's `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household`
    AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`)

§§ `s 6013 -- joint returns; s 1 -- the five tax tables`

-- s 6013(a): "A husband and wife may make a single return jointly ... except ... (1) no joint return shall be made if either
-- the husband or wife at any time during the taxable year is a nonresident alien". (a)(2), different taxable years, cannot
-- arise for two calendar-year taxpayers. The election under s 6013(g), (h) is not encoded.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` ty IF
        `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
    AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`)

-- The table of s 1 (as replaced by s 1(j)(2)) that applies. The names are the Code's own headings.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    -- s 1(a), (j)(2)(A): "Married individuals filing joint returns" (a joint return under s 6013)
    `joint return`
    -- s 1(a)(2), (j)(2)(A): "surviving spouses" (s 2(a))
    `surviving spouse`
    -- s 1(b), (j)(2)(B): "Heads of households" (s 2(b))
    `head of household`
    -- s 1(c), (j)(2)(C): "Unmarried individuals (other than surviving spouses and heads of households)"
    `unmarried individual`
    -- s 1(d), (j)(2)(D): "Married individuals filing separate returns"
    `married filing separately`

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A `Filing status`
DECIDE `the filing status` ty IS
    IF `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`) AND (NOT `treated as not married under s 7703(b)` ty)
    THEN IF ty's `marriage`'s `the spouses make a joint return` AND `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` ty
         THEN `joint return`
         ELSE IF `a head of household under s 2(b)` ty
              THEN `head of household`
              ELSE `married filing separately`
    ELSE IF `a surviving spouse under s 2(a)` ty
         THEN `surviving spouse`
         ELSE IF `a head of household under s 2(b)` ty
              THEN `head of household`
              ELSE `unmarried individual`

GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a joint return or a surviving spouse` s IF s EQUALS `joint return` OR s EQUALS `surviving spouse`

§§ `s 1(j)(2) -- the rate tables, as prescribed for 2026 under s 1(j)(3)(B)`

-- One row of a table: "Over $X but not over $Y | $B, plus R% of the excess over $X".
DECLARE `Rate bracket` HAS
    `over`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the tax at the start of the bracket`                     IS A NUMBER
    `rate`                                                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN o IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rate bracket`
`bracket over` o `tax` b `rate` r MEANS `Rate bracket` WITH
    `over` IS o
    `the tax at the start of the bracket` IS b
    `rate` IS r

-- Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.01, Tables 1 to 4, "For taxable years beginning in 2026". Each row's upper limit is the next row's
-- lower limit. Table 1 (s 1(j)(2)(A)): joint returns and surviving spouses.
`the 2026 table for joint returns and surviving spouses` MEANS LIST
    `bracket over` 0      `tax` 0         `rate` (10%),
    `bracket over` 24800  `tax` 2480      `rate` (12%),
    `bracket over` 100800 `tax` 11600     `rate` (22%),
    `bracket over` 211400 `tax` 35932     `rate` (24%),
    `bracket over` 403550 `tax` 82048     `rate` (32%),
    `bracket over` 512450 `tax` 116896    `rate` (35%),
    `bracket over` 768700 `tax` 206583.50 `rate` (37%)

-- Table 2 (s 1(j)(2)(B)): heads of households.
`the 2026 table for heads of households` MEANS LIST
    `bracket over` 0      `tax` 0         `rate` (10%),
    `bracket over` 17700  `tax` 1770      `rate` (12%),
    `bracket over` 67450  `tax` 7740      `rate` (22%),
    `bracket over` 105700 `tax` 16155     `rate` (24%),
    `bracket over` 201750 `tax` 39207     `rate` (32%),
    `bracket over` 256200 `tax` 56631     `rate` (35%),
    `bracket over` 640600 `tax` 191171    `rate` (37%)

-- Table 3 (s 1(j)(2)(C)): unmarried individuals other than surviving spouses and heads of households.
`the 2026 table for unmarried individuals` MEANS LIST
    `bracket over` 0      `tax` 0         `rate` (10%),
    `bracket over` 12400  `tax` 1240      `rate` (12%),
    `bracket over` 50400  `tax` 5800      `rate` (22%),
    `bracket over` 105700 `tax` 17966     `rate` (24%),
    `bracket over` 201775 `tax` 41024     `rate` (32%),
    `bracket over` 256225 `tax` 58448     `rate` (35%),
    `bracket over` 640600 `tax` 192979.25 `rate` (37%)

-- Table 4 (s 1(j)(2)(D)): married individuals filing separate returns.
`the 2026 table for married individuals filing separately` MEANS LIST
    `bracket over` 0      `tax` 0         `rate` (10%),
    `bracket over` 12400  `tax` 1240      `rate` (12%),
    `bracket over` 50400  `tax` 5800      `rate` (22%),
    `bracket over` 105700 `tax` 17966     `rate` (24%),
    `bracket over` 201775 `tax` 41024     `rate` (32%),
    `bracket over` 256225 `tax` 58448     `rate` (35%),
    `bracket over` 384350 `tax` 103291.75 `rate` (37%)

GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Rate bracket`
`the 2026 rate table for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `joint return`              THEN `the 2026 table for joint returns and surviving spouses`
    WHEN `surviving spouse`          THEN `the 2026 table for joint returns and surviving spouses`
    WHEN `head of household`         THEN `the 2026 table for heads of households`
    WHEN `unmarried individual`      THEN `the 2026 table for unmarried individuals`
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `the 2026 table for married individuals filing separately`

-- The tax on a taxable income: the last row whose "over" amount the income exceeds.
GIVEN `the table` IS A LIST OF `Rate bracket`
      ti IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under` `the table` `on` ti MEANS
    IF ti AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the tax in` (at `the rows exceeded` (count `the rows exceeded` MINUS 1)) `on` ti
    WHERE
        `the rows exceeded` MEANS filter (GIVEN b YIELD ti GREATER THAN b's `over`) `the table`
        GIVEN r IS A `Rate bracket`, i IS A NUMBER
        `the tax in` r `on` i MEANS r's `the tax at the start of the bracket` PLUS (r's `rate` TIMES (i MINUS r's `over`))

-- s 1(a) to (d), (j)(2): the tax imposed on taxable income for 2026. (s 3 tables are not deposited; see NOTES.md.)
GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`, ti IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 tax imposed by s 1 for` s `on` ti MEANS `the tax under` (`the 2026 rate table for` s) `on` ti

§§ `ss 1401, 1402 -- the tax on self-employment income; s 164(f)`

-- s 1402(a), (a)(12): net earnings from self-employment are gross income from the trade or business less its deductions,
-- with, "in lieu of the deduction provided by section 164(f)", a deduction of those earnings times "one-half of the sum of
-- the rates imposed by subsections (a) and (b) of section 1401" (12.4% and 2.9%, so 7.65%).
GIVEN `gross income from the business` IS A NUMBER, `deductions of the business` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`net earnings from self-employment on` `gross income from the business` `less` `deductions of the business` MEANS
    `the earnings before (a)(12)` MINUS (`the earnings before (a)(12)` TIMES (50% TIMES (12.4% PLUS 2.9%)))
    WHERE
        `the earnings before (a)(12)` MEANS `gross income from the business` MINUS `deductions of the business`

-- 42 U.S.C. 430 (s 230 of the Social Security Act), as determined for 2026: "the contribution and benefit base will be
-- $184,500 for remuneration paid in 2026" (SSA, 90 FR 49047, deposited with the Social Security Act subject).
`the 2026 contribution and benefit base` MEANS 184500

-- s 1402(b): self-employment income is net earnings from self-employment, but (2) none if those earnings are under $400,
-- and (1) for the s 1401(a) tax, not the part above the contribution and benefit base less wages paid.
GIVEN nese IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` nese MEANS
    IF nese LESS THAN 400 THEN 0 ELSE nese

GIVEN nese IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`self-employment income for the s 1401(a) tax from` nese `with wages of` wages MEANS
    min (`self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` nese)
        (`the positive part of` (`the 2026 contribution and benefit base` MINUS wages))

-- s 1401(a) 12.4% and (b)(1) 2.9%, for one individual.
GIVEN nese IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes on` nese `with wages of` wages MEANS
        (12.4% TIMES `self-employment income for the s 1401(a) tax from` nese `with wages of` wages)
    PLUS (2.9% TIMES `self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` nese)

-- s 1401(b)(2): 0.9% of self-employment income above $250,000 (joint return), $125,000 (married filing separately) or
-- $200,000, the threshold "reduced (but not below zero) by the amount of wages" taken into account for the s 3101(b)(2) tax.
GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 1401(b)(2) threshold for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `joint return`              THEN 250000
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 125000
    OTHERWISE 200000

GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`, sei IS A NUMBER, wages IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 1401(b)(2) additional tax for` s `on` sei `with wages of` wages MEANS
    0.9% TIMES `the positive part of` (sei MINUS `the positive part of` (`the s 1401(b)(2) threshold for` s MINUS wages))

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxpayer's net earnings from self-employment` ty MEANS
    `net earnings from self-employment on` (ty's `income`'s `business gross income of the taxpayer`)
        `less` (ty's `income`'s `business deductions of the taxpayer`)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse's net earnings from self-employment` ty MEANS
    `net earnings from self-employment on` (ty's `income`'s `business gross income of the spouse`)
        `less` (ty's `income`'s `business deductions of the spouse`)

-- ss 1401(a), (b)(1) for the taxpayer, and for the spouse on a joint return.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes for the year` ty MEANS
        `the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes on` (`the taxpayer's net earnings from self-employment` ty)
            `with wages of` (ty's `income`'s `wages of the taxpayer`)
    PLUS (IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`
          THEN `the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes on` (`the spouse's net earnings from self-employment` ty)
                   `with wages of` (ty's `income`'s `wages of the spouse`)
          ELSE 0)

-- s 1401(b)(2) on the return's self-employment income and wages (the couple's together on a joint return).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 1401(b)(2) tax for the year` ty MEANS
    IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`
    THEN `the s 1401(b)(2) additional tax for` (`the filing status` ty)
             `on` (    `self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` (`the taxpayer's net earnings from self-employment` ty)
                  PLUS `self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` (`the spouse's net earnings from self-employment` ty))
             `with wages of` (ty's `income`'s `wages of the taxpayer` PLUS ty's `income`'s `wages of the spouse`)
    ELSE `the s 1401(b)(2) additional tax for` (`the filing status` ty)
             `on` (`self-employment income for the s 1401(b) tax from` (`the taxpayer's net earnings from self-employment` ty))
             `with wages of` (ty's `income`'s `wages of the taxpayer`)

-- chapter 2: the whole tax on self-employment income.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on self-employment income for the year` ty MEANS
    `the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes for the year` ty PLUS `the s 1401(b)(2) tax for the year` ty

-- s 164(f)(1): "one-half of the taxes imposed by section 1401 (other than the taxes imposed by section 1401(b)(2))"; treated
-- by (f)(2) as attributable to a trade or business, so it is a s 62(a)(1) deduction.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 164(f) deduction` ty MEANS 50% TIMES `the s 1401(a) and (b)(1) taxes for the year` ty

§§ `ss 61, 62, 86 -- gross income and adjusted gross income`

-- The business gross income and deductions on the return (the spouse's only on a joint return).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the business gross income on the return` ty MEANS
    ty's `income`'s `business gross income of the taxpayer`
    PLUS (IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN ty's `income`'s `business gross income of the spouse` ELSE 0)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the business deductions on the return` ty MEANS
    ty's `income`'s `business deductions of the taxpayer`
    PLUS (IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN ty's `income`'s `business deductions of the spouse` ELSE 0)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wages on the return` ty MEANS
    ty's `income`'s `wages of the taxpayer`
    PLUS (IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN ty's `income`'s `wages of the spouse` ELSE 0)

-- s 61(a): gross income other than social security benefits.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`gross income apart from social security benefits` ty MEANS
         `the wages on the return` ty
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `taxable interest`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `ordinary dividends`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `qualified dividends and net capital gain`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `taxable pensions and annuities`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `unemployment compensation`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `other gross income`
    PLUS `the business gross income on the return` ty

-- s 62(a): the deductions taken from gross income: (a)(1) trade or business deductions, including s 164(f), and the others.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductions in arriving at adjusted gross income` ty MEANS
         `the business deductions on the return` ty
    PLUS `the s 164(f) deduction` ty
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `other deductions in arriving at adjusted gross income`

-- s 86(b)(2): modified adjusted gross income is adjusted gross income "determined without regard to this section" (and ss
-- 85(c), 135, 137, 221, 911, 931, 933, none of which is asked), increased by tax-exempt interest.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`modified adjusted gross income for s 86` ty MEANS
        `gross income apart from social security benefits` ty
    MINUS `the deductions in arriving at adjusted gross income` ty
    PLUS  ty's `income`'s `tax-exempt interest`

-- s 86(c): the base amount and the adjusted base amount. Zero for a married individual (s 7703) who does not file a joint
-- return and does not live apart from the spouse at all times during the year.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `described in s 86(c)(1)(C)` ty IF
        `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
    AND (NOT `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 86 base amount` ty MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN 32000
           IF `described in s 86(c)(1)(C)` ty THEN 0
           OTHERWISE 25000

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 86 adjusted base amount` ty MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN 44000
           IF `described in s 86(c)(1)(C)` ty THEN 0
           OTHERWISE 34000

-- s 86(a), (b), on its own inputs so that a Social Security benefit can be tested apart from a return.
GIVEN benefits IS A NUMBER, magi IS A NUMBER, base IS A NUMBER, `adjusted base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the social security benefits included in gross income under s 86 on` benefits `with modified AGI` magi `base amount` base `adjusted base amount` `adjusted base` MEANS
    -- (a)(2): the lesser of (A) 85% of the excess over the adjusted base amount plus the lesser of the (a)(1) amount and
    -- half the difference between the two base amounts, or (B) 85% of the benefits
    BRANCH IF `the s 86(b)(1)(A) sum` AT MOST base THEN 0
           IF `the s 86(b)(1)(A) sum` GREATER THAN `adjusted base`
               THEN min (    (85% TIMES (`the s 86(b)(1)(A) sum` MINUS `adjusted base`))
                         PLUS (min `the s 86(a)(1) amount` (50% TIMES (`adjusted base` MINUS base))))
                        (85% TIMES benefits)
           OTHERWISE `the s 86(a)(1) amount`
    WHERE
        -- (b)(1)(A): modified adjusted gross income plus one-half of the benefits
        `the s 86(b)(1)(A) sum` MEANS magi PLUS (50% TIMES benefits)
        -- (a)(1): the lesser of one-half of the benefits or one-half of the excess over the base amount
        `the s 86(a)(1) amount` MEANS min (50% TIMES benefits) (50% TIMES (`the s 86(b)(1)(A) sum` MINUS base))

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable social security benefits` ty MEANS
    `the social security benefits included in gross income under s 86 on` (ty's `income`'s `social security benefits`)
        `with modified AGI` (`modified adjusted gross income for s 86` ty)
        `base amount` (`the s 86 base amount` ty)
        `adjusted base amount` (`the s 86 adjusted base amount` ty)

-- s 61(a), s 86(a): gross income.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`gross income` ty MEANS `gross income apart from social security benefits` ty PLUS `the taxable social security benefits` ty

-- s 62(a): adjusted gross income.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`adjusted gross income` ty MEANS `gross income` ty MINUS `the deductions in arriving at adjusted gross income` ty

-- s 32(c)(2)(A): earned income: wages includible in gross income, plus net earnings from self-employment "determined with
-- regard to the deduction allowed to the taxpayer by section 164(f)". Read as: the business profit less the s 164(f)
-- deduction (NOTES.md finding 6). (c)(2)(B)(ii): no pension or annuity counts. On a joint return, both spouses'.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`earned income` ty MEANS
         `the wages on the return` ty
    PLUS `the business gross income on the return` ty
    MINUS `the business deductions on the return` ty
    MINUS `the s 164(f) deduction` ty

§§ `s 63 -- the standard deduction and taxable income`

-- s 63(c)(2) as adjusted by s 63(c)(7) and Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.14(1), for 2026.
GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 basic standard deduction for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `joint return`              THEN 32200
    WHEN `surviving spouse`          THEN 32200
    WHEN `head of household`         THEN 24150
    WHEN `unmarried individual`      THEN 16100
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 16100

-- s 63(c)(5), Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.14(2): an individual whom another taxpayer may claim gets no more than the greater of
-- $1,350 or $450 plus earned income.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic standard deduction` ty MEANS
    IF ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`
    THEN min (`the 2026 basic standard deduction for` (`the filing status` ty)) (max 1350 (450 PLUS `earned income` ty))
    ELSE `the 2026 basic standard deduction for` (`the filing status` ty)

-- s 63(f)(3), Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.14(3): each additional amount is $1,650, or $2,050 for an individual who is not
-- married and not a surviving spouse.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 additional amount for the aged or blind` ty MEANS
    IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `unmarried individual` OR `the filing status` ty EQUALS `head of household`
    THEN 2050
    ELSE 1650

-- s 151(b): an exemption for the spouse where no joint return is made, the spouse has no gross income and is not the
-- dependent of another taxpayer. s 63(f)(1)(B), (2)(B) give the spouse's additional amounts only in that case.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an additional exemption is allowable for the spouse under s 151(b)` ty IF
        `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
    AND (NOT `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse has gross income`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`)

-- s 63(f)(1), (2): the number of additional amounts. On a joint return each spouse is the taxpayer (s 6013(d)(3)), so each
-- spouse's age and blindness count under (A) (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of additional amounts for age` ty MEANS
    (IF ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65 THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF (`the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` OR `an additional exemption is allowable for the spouse under s 151(b)` ty)
             AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65
          THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of additional amounts for blindness` ty MEANS
    (IF ty's `the taxpayer is blind` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF (`the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` OR `an additional exemption is allowable for the spouse under s 151(b)` ty)
             AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse is blind`
          THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- s 63(c)(3), (f)
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional standard deduction` ty MEANS
    `the 2026 additional amount for the aged or blind` ty
        TIMES (`the number of additional amounts for age` ty PLUS `the number of additional amounts for blindness` ty)

-- s 63(c)(1), (6)(A): the standard deduction; zero for a married individual filing separately where either spouse
-- itemizes. (A nonresident alien, (c)(6)(B), is not covered.)
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard deduction` ty MEANS
    IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `married filing separately`
       AND (ty's `income`'s `the taxpayer elects to itemize` OR ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the basic standard deduction` ty PLUS `the additional standard deduction` ty

-- s 151(d)(5)(C): $6,000 for each qualified individual (the taxpayer, and on a joint return the spouse, aged 65 before the
-- close of the year), reduced by 6% of modified adjusted gross income above $75,000 ($150,000 joint); the social security
-- number must be on the return; a married individual (s 7703) must file jointly. For taxable years beginning before 2029.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of qualified individuals for the deduction for seniors` ty MEANS
    (IF     ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65
        AND ty's `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment`
     THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF     `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`
             AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65
             AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment`
          THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction for seniors under s 151(d)(5)(C)` ty MEANS
    IF `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`) AND (NOT `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the number of qualified individuals for the deduction for seniors` ty
             TIMES `the positive part of` (6000 MINUS (6% TIMES `the positive part of` (`adjusted gross income` ty MINUS `the threshold`)))
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN 150000 ELSE 75000

-- s 151(d)(5)(A): "the term 'exemption amount' means zero", so the s 151(b), (c) exemptions are nil; s 151's only deduction
-- left is the deduction for seniors.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under s 151` ty MEANS `the deduction for seniors under s 151(d)(5)(C)` ty

-- s 63(b), (e): the deduction taken from adjusted gross income: the standard deduction, or (if elected) itemized deductions.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard or itemized deduction` ty MEANS
    IF ty's `income`'s `the taxpayer elects to itemize`
    THEN ty's `income`'s `itemized deductions`
    ELSE `the standard deduction` ty

-- s 63(a), (b): taxable income (not below zero).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`taxable income` ty MEANS
    `the positive part of` (     `adjusted gross income` ty
                           MINUS `the standard or itemized deduction` ty
                           MINUS `the deduction under s 151` ty
                           MINUS ty's `income`'s `other deductions allowed to a non-itemizer`)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regular tax` ty MEANS `the 2026 tax imposed by s 1 for` (`the filing status` ty) `on` (`taxable income` ty)

§§ `s 55 -- a screen for the alternative minimum tax`

-- Not an encoding of s 55: an upper bound on alternative minimum taxable income for the facts this encoding takes, with
-- every deduction below adjusted gross income added back and all tax-exempt interest treated as a preference. If the
-- tentative minimum tax on that bound is no more than the regular tax, the s 55(a) tax is zero. Otherwise: not covered.
-- Figures: Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.10.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`an upper bound on alternative minimum taxable income` ty MEANS
         `taxable income` ty
    PLUS `the standard or itemized deduction` ty
    PLUS `the deduction under s 151` ty
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `other deductions allowed to a non-itemizer`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `tax-exempt interest`

-- s 55(d)(1), (d)(4) as adjusted for 2026: $140,200, $90,100, $70,100; phased out at 50% above $1,000,000 or $500,000.
GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`, amti IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 AMT exemption amount for` s `on` amti MEANS
    `the positive part of` (`the amount` MINUS (50% TIMES `the positive part of` (amti MINUS `the threshold`)))
    WHERE
        `the amount` MEANS
            BRANCH IF `a joint return or a surviving spouse` s THEN 140200
                   IF s EQUALS `married filing separately` THEN 70100
                   OTHERWISE 90100
        `the threshold` MEANS IF `a joint return or a surviving spouse` s THEN 1000000 ELSE 500000

-- s 55(b)(1)(A), (C): 26% up to $244,500 of taxable excess ($122,250 married filing separately), 28% above.
GIVEN s IS A `Filing status`, amti IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 tentative minimum tax for` s `on` amti MEANS
    (26% TIMES min `the taxable excess` `the 28 percent point`)
    PLUS (28% TIMES `the positive part of` (`the taxable excess` MINUS `the 28 percent point`))
    WHERE
        `the taxable excess` MEANS `the positive part of` (amti MINUS `the 2026 AMT exemption amount for` s `on` amti)
        `the 28 percent point` MEANS IF s EQUALS `married filing separately` THEN 122250 ELSE 244500

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the alternative minimum tax is screened out` ty IF
        `the 2026 tentative minimum tax for` (`the filing status` ty) `on` (`an upper bound on alternative minimum taxable income` ty)
            AT MOST `the regular tax` ty
    AND (    (NOT `the filing status` ty EQUALS `married filing separately`)
         -- s 55(d)(2), last sentence, raises a separate filer's AMTI above $640,200; not bounded here
         OR  `an upper bound on alternative minimum taxable income` ty AT MOST 640200)

§§ `s 24 -- the Child Tax Credit and the credit for other dependents`

-- s 24(a), (c), (h)(7): a qualifying child (s 152(c)) under 17, who passes the s 24(c)(2) citizenship test, for whom the
-- taxpayer is allowed a s 151 deduction (a dependent), with a social security number on the return. (h)(7)(A)(i): the
-- taxpayer's own number (on a joint return, at least one spouse's) must be on the return too.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying child under s 24(c)` ty p IF
        `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`) TRUE
    AND p's `age at the close of the year` LESS THAN 17
    AND `meets the s 24 citizenship or residence test` p
    AND `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taxpayer's social security number requirement in s 24(h)(7)(A)(i) is met` ty IF
        ty's `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment`
    OR  (`the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment`)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying child for whom the s 24 credit is allowed` ty p IF
        `a qualifying child under s 24(c)` ty p
    AND p's `has a social security number valid for employment`
    AND `the taxpayer's social security number requirement in s 24(h)(7)(A)(i) is met` ty

-- s 24(h)(4): $500 for each dependent other than a qualifying child described in s 24(c), passing the s 24 citizenship
-- test; (h)(4)(C): a qualifying child denied the credit by (h)(7) counts here instead.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dependent for the s 24(h)(4) partial credit` ty p IF
        `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p
    AND `meets the s 24 citizenship or residence test` p
    AND (NOT `a qualifying child for whom the s 24 credit is allowed` ty p)

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of qualifying children for the s 24 credit` ty MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `a qualifying child for whom the s 24 credit is allowed` ty p) (ty's `people`))

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of other dependents for the s 24 credit` ty MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `a dependent for the s 24(h)(4) partial credit` ty p) (ty's `people`))

-- s 24(a), (h)(2), (i)(2) and Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.05(1): $2,200 for 2026; (h)(4)(A): $500.
`the 2026 credit per qualifying child` MEANS 2200
`the credit per other dependent` MEANS 500

-- s 24(b)(1), (h)(3): reduced by $50 for each $1,000 (or fraction) of modified adjusted gross income above $400,000 (joint
-- return) or $200,000. Modified AGI adds back ss 911, 931, 933 exclusions, which are not asked.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 24(b) reduction` ty MEANS
    50 TIMES CEILING (`the positive part of` (`adjusted gross income` ty MINUS `the threshold`) DIVIDED BY 1000)
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS IF `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return` THEN 400000 ELSE 200000

-- The s 24 credit before the s 26(a) limitation and before subsection (d).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 24 credit before the tax limitation` ty MEANS
    `the positive part of` (     (`the 2026 credit per qualifying child` TIMES `the number of qualifying children for the s 24 credit` ty)
                            PLUS (`the credit per other dependent` TIMES `the number of other dependents for the s 24 credit` ty)
                            MINUS `the s 24(b) reduction` ty)

-- s 26(a): the subpart A credits may not exceed the regular tax liability (plus the s 55 tax, zero where covered). No
-- other subpart A credit is asked, so the s 24 credit is the only one.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 24 credit allowed against the tax` ty MEANS min (`the s 24 credit before the tax limitation` ty) (`the regular tax` ty)

-- s 24(d)(2): social security taxes are the s 3101 taxes withheld (asked) plus 50% of the s 1401 taxes.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the social security taxes under s 24(d)(2)` ty MEANS
    ty's `income`'s `social security taxes withheld from wages` PLUS (50% TIMES `the tax on self-employment income for the year` ty)

-- s 24(d)(1), (h)(5), (h)(6), (i)(1) and Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.05(2): the refundable portion is the lesser of
-- (A) the credit without (d) and s 26(a), capped at $1,700 per qualifying child and computed without the (h)(4) amount, and
-- (B) the increase in the credit if the s 26(a) limit rose by the greater of 15% of earned income above $2,500 or, with 3 or
--     more qualifying children, the social security taxes less the s 32 credit.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refundable portion of the s 24 credit under s 24(d)` ty MEANS
    min `limb (A)` `limb (B)`
    WHERE
        `the qualifying children` MEANS `the number of qualifying children for the s 24 credit` ty
        `limb (A)` MEANS
            min (`the positive part of` ((`the 2026 credit per qualifying child` TIMES `the qualifying children`) MINUS `the s 24(b) reduction` ty))
                (1700 TIMES `the qualifying children`)
        `the increase in the limitation` MEANS
            max (15% TIMES `the positive part of` (`earned income` ty MINUS 2500))
                (IF `the qualifying children` AT LEAST 3
                 THEN `the positive part of` (`the social security taxes under s 24(d)(2)` ty MINUS `the s 32 credit` ty)
                 ELSE 0)
        `limb (B)` MEANS
            min (`the s 24 credit before the tax limitation` ty MINUS `the s 24 credit allowed against the tax` ty)
                `the increase in the limitation`

§§ `s 32 -- the earned income credit`

-- s 32(c)(3): a qualifying child for s 32 is a s 152(c) qualifying child determined without the support test and s 152(e),
-- (B) not married unless the taxpayer may claim them, (C) with the home in the United States. (D), (m): counted in
-- subsection (b) only with a social security number on the return.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying child under s 32(c)(3)` ty p IF
        `a qualifying child under s 152(c)` p (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`) FALSE
    AND ((NOT p's `married at the close of the year`) OR `a dependent of the taxpayer` ty p)
    AND p's `the shared home was in the United States`

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of qualifying children under s 32(b)` ty MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `a qualifying child under s 32(c)(3)` ty p AND p's `has a social security number valid for employment`) (ty's `people`))

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taxpayer has a qualifying child under s 32` ty IF
    any (GIVEN p YIELD `a qualifying child under s 32(c)(3)` ty p) (ty's `people`)

-- s 32(c)(1)(A): an eligible individual has a qualifying child, or (ii) has none and lives in the United States for more than
-- half the year, is (or, if married, the spouse is) aged 25 to 64, and is not another's dependent. (B): not if a qualifying
-- child of another taxpayer. (E), (m): the taxpayer's (and a spouse's) social security number on the return.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible individual under s 32(c)(1)` ty IF
        (    `the taxpayer has a qualifying child under s 32` ty
         OR  (    ty's `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year`
              AND (    `aged 25 to 64` (ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`)
                   OR  (    `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
                        AND `aged 25 to 64` (ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse's age at the close of the year`)))
              AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`)))
    AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`)
    AND (NOT ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`)
    AND ty's `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment`
    AND (    (NOT `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`))
         OR  ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment`)
    WHERE
        GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
        `aged 25 to 64` age MEANS age AT LEAST 25 AND age LESS THAN 65

-- s 32(d): a married individual gets the credit only on a joint return, unless (d)(2)(B): not filing jointly, living with a
-- qualifying child for more than half the year, and not sharing a home with the spouse in the last 6 months. (The
-- separation-agreement limb, (B)(iii)(II), is not encoded.)
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 32(d) joint return condition is met` ty IF
        (NOT `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`))
    OR  `the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`
    OR  (    `the taxpayer has a qualifying child under s 32` ty
         AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year`))

-- s 32(i)(2)(A), (B): disqualified income (interest, dividends, tax-exempt interest; capital gain is not covered).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`disqualified income under s 32(i)` ty MEANS
    ty's `income`'s `taxable interest` PLUS ty's `income`'s `tax-exempt interest` PLUS ty's `income`'s `ordinary dividends`
    PLUS ty's `income`'s `qualified dividends and net capital gain`

-- s 32(b)(1): the credit and phaseout percentages.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 32 credit percentage with qualifying children numbering` n MEANS
    BRANCH IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 7.65%
           IF n EQUALS 1 THEN 34%
           IF n EQUALS 2 THEN 40%
           OTHERWISE 45%

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 32 phaseout percentage with qualifying children numbering` n MEANS
    BRANCH IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 7.65%
           IF n EQUALS 1 THEN 15.98%
           OTHERWISE 21.06%

-- s 32(b)(2), (j) and Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.06(1): the 2026 earned income amounts and phaseout amounts (the joint figures
-- include the (b)(2)(B) increase).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 earned income amount with qualifying children numbering` n MEANS
    BRANCH IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 8680
           IF n EQUALS 1 THEN 13020
           OTHERWISE 18290

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, joint IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 phaseout amount with qualifying children numbering` n `on a joint return` joint MEANS
    BRANCH IF joint AND n EQUALS 0 THEN 18140
           IF joint THEN 31160
           IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 10860
           OTHERWISE 23890

-- s 32(i)(1), (j) and Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.06(2): $12,200 for 2026.
`the 2026 disqualified income limit` MEANS 12200

-- s 32(a): the credit percentage of earned income up to the earned income amount, but no more than the credit percentage of
-- the earned income amount less the phaseout percentage of adjusted gross income (or, if greater, earned income) above the
-- phaseout amount.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, joint IS A BOOLEAN, ei IS A NUMBER, agi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 32(a) amount with qualifying children numbering` n `on a joint return` joint `on earned income` ei `and AGI` agi MEANS
    `the positive part of` (min `the (a)(1) amount` `the (a)(2) limitation`)
    WHERE
        `the (a)(1) amount` MEANS
            `the s 32 credit percentage with qualifying children numbering` n
                TIMES min (`the positive part of` ei) (`the 2026 earned income amount with qualifying children numbering` n)
        `the (a)(2) limitation` MEANS
            (`the s 32 credit percentage with qualifying children numbering` n TIMES `the 2026 earned income amount with qualifying children numbering` n)
            MINUS (`the s 32 phaseout percentage with qualifying children numbering` n
                       TIMES `the positive part of` (max agi ei MINUS `the 2026 phaseout amount with qualifying children numbering` n `on a joint return` joint))

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 32 credit` ty MEANS
    IF     `an eligible individual under s 32(c)(1)` ty
       AND `the s 32(d) joint return condition is met` ty
       AND `disqualified income under s 32(i)` ty AT MOST `the 2026 disqualified income limit`
    THEN `the s 32(a) amount with qualifying children numbering` (`the number of qualifying children under s 32(b)` ty)
             `on a joint return` (`the filing status` ty EQUALS `joint return`)
             `on earned income` (`earned income` ty) `and AGI` (`adjusted gross income` ty)
    ELSE 0

§§ `The return: tax, credits, and the balance`

DECLARE `Return figures` HAS
    `filing status`                                           IS A `Filing status`
    `gross income`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `taxable social security benefits`                        IS A NUMBER
    `adjusted gross income`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `standard or itemized deduction`                          IS A NUMBER
    `deduction for seniors`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `income tax under s 1`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `child tax credit against the tax`                        IS A NUMBER
    `tax on self-employment income`                           IS A NUMBER
    `total tax`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `refundable child tax credit`                             IS A NUMBER
    `earned income credit`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `income tax withheld`                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- positive: the amount still to pay; negative: an overpayment (refund) of that size
    `balance due`                                             IS A NUMBER

-- The gaps, in the order they are tested.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the gap in` ty MEANS
    -- s 1(g)(2), (4): a child with net unearned income above twice the s 63(c)(5)(A) amount ($1,350 x 2 for 2026) is tested
    -- for any taxpayer another may claim, as an upper bound (the age and parent conditions are not asked).
    BRANCH IF (NOT ty's `the calendar year` EQUALS 2026)
               THEN JUST `the figures of a taxable year other than 2026 are not deposited`
           IF ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`
               THEN JUST `a nonresident alien is taxed under s 871 and s 877, which are not encoded`
           IF (NOT ty's `income`'s `qualified dividends and net capital gain` EQUALS 0)
               THEN JUST `net capital gain and qualified dividends are taxed under s 1(h), which is not encoded`
           IF ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer` AND (`gross income` ty MINUS `earned income` ty) GREATER THAN 2700
               THEN JUST `the s 1(g) tax on a child's unearned income is not encoded`
           IF (NOT `the alternative minimum tax is screened out` ty)
               THEN JUST `the alternative minimum tax under s 55 may apply, and it is not encoded beyond a screen`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A `Return figures`
`the figures of the return` ty MEANS `Return figures` WITH
    `filing status`                    IS `the filing status` ty
    `gross income`                     IS `gross income` ty
    `taxable social security benefits` IS `the taxable social security benefits` ty
    `adjusted gross income`            IS `adjusted gross income` ty
    `standard or itemized deduction`   IS `the standard or itemized deduction` ty
    `deduction for seniors`            IS `the deduction for seniors under s 151(d)(5)(C)` ty
    `taxable income`                   IS `taxable income` ty
    `income tax under s 1`             IS `the regular tax` ty
    `child tax credit against the tax` IS `the s 24 credit allowed against the tax` ty
    `tax on self-employment income`    IS `the tax on self-employment income for the year` ty
    `total tax`                        IS `the total tax`
    `refundable child tax credit`      IS `the refundable portion of the s 24 credit under s 24(d)` ty
    `earned income credit`             IS `the s 32 credit` ty
    `income tax withheld`              IS ty's `income`'s `income tax withheld`
    `balance due`                      IS     `the total tax`
                                        MINUS `the refundable portion of the s 24 credit under s 24(d)` ty
                                        MINUS `the s 32 credit` ty
                                        MINUS ty's `income`'s `income tax withheld`
    WHERE
        -- chapter 1 tax less the s 24 credit allowed against it, plus chapter 2 tax (the s 24 credit is "against the tax
        -- imposed by this chapter", chapter 1, so it does not reduce the tax on self-employment income)
        `the total tax` MEANS
            (`the regular tax` ty MINUS `the s 24 credit allowed against the tax` ty) PLUS `the tax on self-employment income for the year` ty

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Return figures`
`the return for the year` ty MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap in` ty
    WHEN JUST reason THEN `not covered` reason
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`the figures of the return` ty)

§§ `s 6012 -- who must make a return`

-- s 6012(a)(1)(D)(ii): "The term 'exemption amount' has the meaning given such term by section 151(d)." For 2026,
-- s 151(d)(5)(A): "The term 'exemption amount' means zero." s 6012(f), the 2018-2025 rule, no longer applies. The IRS uses
-- the indexed amount ($5,300) for s 152(d)(1)(B) (Rev. Proc. 2025-32 s 4.23), and s 151(d)(5)(B) keeps the zero from
-- deciding whether a deduction is allowed. Whether s 6012 reads zero or $5,300 is not settled by the deposited text
-- (NOTES.md finding 1), so both readings are encoded and the answer says when they differ.
DECLARE `Reading of the exemption amount in s 6012` IS ONE OF
    `zero, as s 151(d)(5)(A) states`
    `the indexed amount of $5,300 used for s 152(d)(1)(B)`

GIVEN r IS A `Reading of the exemption amount in s 6012`, ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exemption amount for s 6012 on the reading` r ty MEANS
    -- (D)(ii): "In the case of an individual described in section 151(d)(2), the exemption amount shall be zero."
    IF ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `zero, as s 151(d)(5)(A) states` THEN 0
         WHEN `the indexed amount of $5,300 used for s 152(d)(1)(B)` THEN `the 2026 exemption amount referred to in s 152(d)(1)(B)`

-- s 6012(a)(1)(B): for clauses (i) to (iii), one additional standard deduction for an individual aged 65 or more; for clause
-- (iv), each additional standard deduction of the individual or the spouse by reason of s 63(f)(1).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a single return` ty MEANS
    IF ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65
    THEN `the 2026 additional amount for the aged or blind` ty
    ELSE 0

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a joint return` ty MEANS
    1650 TIMES (    (IF ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65 THEN 1 ELSE 0)
                PLUS (IF ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse's age at the close of the year` AT LEAST 65 THEN 1 ELSE 0))

-- s 6012(a)(1)(A)(iv): entitled to make a joint return, combined gross income less than twice the exemption amount plus the
-- joint basic standard deduction, the same household at the close of the year; not where the spouse makes a separate return
-- or another taxpayer is entitled to an exemption for the spouse.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `clause (iv) can apply` ty IF
        `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` ty
    AND ty's `marriage`'s `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year`
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse makes a separate return`)
    AND (NOT ty's `marriage`'s `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`)

-- s 6012(a)(1)(C): for an individual described in s 63(c)(5) (one another may claim), the exceptions do not apply if
-- (I) unearned income exceeds $1,350 plus any additional standard deduction, or (II) gross income exceeds the standard
-- deduction.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exceptions are shut off by s 6012(a)(1)(C)` ty IF
        ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`
    AND (    (`gross income` ty MINUS `earned income` ty) GREATER THAN (1350 PLUS `the additional standard deduction` ty)
         OR  `gross income` ty GREATER THAN `the standard deduction` ty)

GIVEN m IS A `Marriage`
GIVETH A `Marriage`
`the marriage with a joint return made` m MEANS `Marriage` WITH
    `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death` IS m's `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death`
    `the spouse died during the year`                         IS m's `the spouse died during the year`
    `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance` IS m's `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance`
    `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS m's `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`
    `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year` IS m's `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year`
    `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`    IS m's `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`
    `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year` IS m's `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year`
    `the spouses make a joint return`                         IS TRUE
    `the spouse makes a separate return`                      IS m's `the spouse makes a separate return`
    `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`     IS m's `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`
    `the spouse's age at the close of the year`               IS m's `the spouse's age at the close of the year`
    `the spouse is blind`                                     IS m's `the spouse is blind`
    `the spouse has gross income`                             IS m's `the spouse has gross income`
    `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`         IS m's `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`
    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS m's `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment`
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS m's `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS m's `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS m's `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death`

-- The gross income compared under clause (iv): the couple's combined gross income, as on a joint return.
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A `Taxable year`
`the year as if a joint return were made` ty MEANS `Taxable year` WITH
    `the calendar year`                                       IS ty's `the calendar year`
    `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`             IS ty's `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`
    `the taxpayer is blind`                                   IS ty's `the taxpayer is blind`
    `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`
    `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`         IS ty's `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`
    `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`  IS ty's `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`
    `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment` IS ty's `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment`
    `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year` IS ty's `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year`
    `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household` IS ty's `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household`
    `marriage`                                                IS `the marriage with a joint return made` (ty's `marriage`)
    `people`                                                  IS ty's `people`
    `income`                                                  IS ty's `income`

-- s 6012(a)(1)(A): a return is required of an individual whose gross income equals or exceeds the exemption amount, unless
-- an exception (i) to (iv) applies.
GIVEN r IS A `Reading of the exemption amount in s 6012`, ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a return is required by s 6012(a)(1) on the reading` r ty IF
        `gross income` ty AT LEAST `the exemption amount`
    AND (NOT `an exception applies`)
    WHERE
        `the exemption amount` MEANS `the exemption amount for s 6012 on the reading` r ty
        `the status` MEANS `the filing status` ty
        `an exception applies` MEANS
                (NOT `the exceptions are shut off by s 6012(a)(1)(C)` ty)
            AND (    -- (i) not married (s 7703), not a surviving spouse, not a head of household
                     (    (NOT `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`))
                      AND (NOT `a surviving spouse under s 2(a)` ty)
                      AND (NOT `a head of household under s 2(b)` ty)
                      AND `gross income` ty LESS THAN (`the exemption amount` PLUS `the basic standard deduction` ty PLUS `the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a single return` ty))
                     -- (ii) a head of household
                 OR  (    `a head of household under s 2(b)` ty
                      AND `gross income` ty LESS THAN (`the exemption amount` PLUS 24150 PLUS `the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a single return` ty))
                     -- (iii) a surviving spouse
                 OR  (    `a surviving spouse under s 2(a)` ty
                      AND `gross income` ty LESS THAN (`the exemption amount` PLUS 32200 PLUS `the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a single return` ty))
                     -- (iv) entitled to make a joint return, on the couple's combined gross income
                 OR  (    `clause (iv) can apply` ty
                      AND `gross income` (`the year as if a joint return were made` ty)
                              LESS THAN ((2 TIMES `the exemption amount`) PLUS 32200 PLUS `the s 6012(a)(1)(B) increase for a joint return` ty)))

DECLARE `Whether a return is required` IS ONE OF
    `a return is required`
    `no return is required`
    -- the two readings of "exemption amount" give different answers
    `a return is required if the exemption amount in s 6012 is zero, but not if it is $5,300`
    `not required by s 6012, but s 6017 (self-employment income), which is not deposited, may require one`

GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Whether a return is required`
`whether s 6012 requires a return` ty MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT ty's `the calendar year` EQUALS 2026)
               THEN `not covered` `the figures of a taxable year other than 2026 are not deposited`
           IF ty's `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year`
               THEN `not covered` `a nonresident alien is taxed under s 871 and s 877, which are not encoded`
           IF `on the zero reading` AND `on the indexed reading`
               THEN `answered` `a return is required`
           IF `on the zero reading`
               THEN `answered` `a return is required if the exemption amount in s 6012 is zero, but not if it is $5,300`
           IF `the net earnings from self-employment on the return` AT LEAST 400
               THEN `answered` `not required by s 6012, but s 6017 (self-employment income), which is not deposited, may require one`
           OTHERWISE `answered` `no return is required`
    WHERE
        `on the zero reading` MEANS `a return is required by s 6012(a)(1) on the reading` `zero, as s 151(d)(5)(A) states` ty
        `on the indexed reading` MEANS `a return is required by s 6012(a)(1) on the reading` `the indexed amount of $5,300 used for s 152(d)(1)(B)` ty
        `the net earnings from self-employment on the return` MEANS
            max (`the taxpayer's net earnings from self-employment` ty) (`the spouse's net earnings from self-employment` ty)

§§ `Duties and permissions: making the return`

-- The actors the text names. s 6012(a): "Returns ... shall be made by ... every individual"; (b)(1): a deceased
-- individual's return "shall be made by his executor, administrator, or other person charged with the property"; (b)(2):
-- for an individual unable to make it, "by a duly authorized agent, his committee, guardian, fiduciary or other person
-- charged with the care of the person or property". s 6013: "A husband and wife".
DECLARE `Person who acts` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the executor, administrator or other person charged with the decedent's property`
    `the authorized agent, committee, guardian or fiduciary of an individual unable to make a return`
    `the husband and wife`

DECLARE `Act on a return` IS ONE OF
    -- s 6012(a), (d): the return must include the year's tax-exempt interest
    `make the return of income` HAS `showing the tax-exempt interest received or accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6013(a)
    `make a single return jointly`
    -- s 6013(b)(1): after a separate return
    `make a joint return after filing a separate return`

DECLARE `Situation of the individual` IS ONE OF
    `living and able to make a return`
    `deceased`
    `unable to make a return`

-- s 6012(b)(1), (2): who makes the return.
GIVEN sit IS A `Situation of the individual`
GIVETH A `Person who acts`
`who makes the return` sit MEANS
    CONSIDER sit
    WHEN `living and able to make a return` THEN `the individual`
    WHEN `deceased`                         THEN `the executor, administrator or other person charged with the decedent's property`
    WHEN `unable to make a return`          THEN `the authorized agent, committee, guardian or fiduciary of an individual unable to make a return`

-- s 6012(a), (b), (d): the duty to make a return, counted in days from the close of the taxable year. The day the return is
-- due is set by s 6072, which is not deposited, so it is a parameter. If no return is required, nothing is owed.
GIVEN required IS A BOOLEAN, sit IS A `Situation of the individual`, `days to the due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person who acts` `Act on a return`
`the duty to make a return` required sit `days to the due date` MEANS
    IF required
    THEN PARTY `who makes the return` sit
         MUST  `make the return of income` shows PROVIDED shows
         WITHIN `days to the due date`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY (`who makes the return` sit) BECAUSE "no return of income, showing tax-exempt interest, was made by the day s 6072 sets (s 6012(a), (b), (d))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 6013(a): the husband and wife may make a single return jointly; if either is a nonresident alien at any time in the
-- year, "no joint return shall be made".
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, `days to the due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person who acts` `Act on a return`
`the permission to make a joint return` ty `days to the due date` MEANS
    IF `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` ty
    THEN PARTY `the husband and wife`
         MAY   `make a single return jointly`
         WITHIN `days to the due date`
    ELSE IF `married under s 7703(a)` (ty's `marriage`)
         THEN PARTY `the husband and wife`
              SHANT `make a single return jointly`
              WITHIN `days to the due date`
              LEST  BREACH BY `the husband and wife` BECAUSE "a joint return was made although a spouse was a nonresident alien during the year (s 6013(a)(1))"
         ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 6013(b)(1), (2)(A): after a separate return, the spouses may still make a joint return, but not "after the expiration of
-- 3 years from the last date prescribed by law for filing the return for such taxable year (determined without regard to
-- any extension)". The bars in (2)(B) to (D) are asked as one fact. Counted in days from the due date; the length of the
-- three years in days is worked out from the calendar in irc-dates.l4 (kept apart because the daydate library slows the
-- checking of this module's arithmetic).
GIVEN ty IS A `Taxable year`, `a bar in s 6013(b)(2)(B) to (D) applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `days in the three years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person who acts` `Act on a return`
`the permission to switch to a joint return` ty `a bar in s 6013(b)(2)(B) to (D) applies` `days in the three years` MEANS
    IF `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` ty AND (NOT `a bar in s 6013(b)(2)(B) to (D) applies`)
    THEN PARTY `the husband and wife`
         MAY   `make a joint return after filing a separate return`
         WITHIN `days in the three years`
    ELSE FULFILLED
